# Tyk AI Studio companion stack - private values for the containers.
#
# THIS EXAMPLE IS COMMITTED and ships with every value empty. The generator
# copies it to ./secret.env with fresh values filled in; ./secret.env is the
# private copy: gitignored, mode 0600, and an env_file of both containers.
# The admin login is NOT here: it lives in ./admin.env (see admin.env.example),
# which only the host scripts read, so the password never enters a container.
#
# ===========================================================================
#  TYK AI STUDIO 2.3 ENTERPRISE LICENCE REQUIRED.
# ===========================================================================
# The Model Router, guardrails, budgets, the audit trail and the Tyk Dashboard
# MCP integration are Enterprise features
# (https://tyk.io/docs/ai-management/ai-studio/overview), so without an
# Enterprise licence this directory has nothing to show and ./start.sh refuses
# to start. Both containers read TYK_AI_LICENSE (the control plane and the edge
# each validate it at startup).
#
# Paste the licence into ./secret.env, not into this example: the example is
# committed, so never put a real licence, token or password here.
TYK_AI_LICENSE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared control-plane <-> edge secrets.
#
# The generator mints a fresh matched set per bundle. GRPC_AUTH_TOKEN and
# EDGE_AUTH_TOKEN are two names for the same value (control side and edge side);
# so are MICROGATEWAY_ENCRYPTION_KEY and ENCRYPTION_KEY. If a pair stops
# matching, the edge cannot work with the control plane; start.sh checks both
# pairs before it starts anything.
#
# These live in ./secret.env rather than in confs/ for two reasons: ./secret.env
# is gitignored (confs/ is committed), and env_file entries later in the list
# win, so a value in confs/ would silently override the minted one. Never copy
# fixed values from an example configuration: mint fresh ones per stack.
#
# ENCRYPTION_KEY must be exactly 32 characters.
GRPC_AUTH_TOKEN=
EDGE_AUTH_TOKEN=
MICROGATEWAY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
ENCRYPTION_KEY=
JWT_SECRET=

# Used by the control plane to encrypt stored secrets and SSO state, and by the
# Enterprise Tyk MCP integration to encrypt the Dashboard access token at rest.
TYK_AI_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prometheus scrape token, shared by the control plane and the edge. Scrape with
#   Authorization: Bearer ${METRICS_AUTH_TOKEN}
# AISTUDIO-METRICS-001 proves both planes answer 200 with it and 401 without.
METRICS_AUTH_TOKEN=
